(go/type Type "A Type represents a Go type.\n\nThere may be multiple unnamed types with identical structure. However, there must\nbe a unique Type object for each unique named (defined) type. After noding, a\npackage-level type can be looked up by building its unique symbol sym (sym =\npackage.Lookup(name)) and checking sym.Def. If sym.Def is non-nil, the type\nalready exists at package scope and is available at sym.Def.(*ir.Name).Type().\nLocal types (which may have the same name as a package-level type) are\ndistinguished by their vargen, which is embedded in their symbol name.\n" (struct
















